The correct answer is __**Columns**__.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/36f36cd5ece4186095afcf2ffbfb7b80cc04b6c2e3226e7477a419a9fbc96f85.png] **__Key Points__**

__

• The **Home ribbon** in Microsoft Excel includes a variety of commands and features for formatting and editing cells.

• The Home ribbon contains options for font settings, such as **Font color**, **Bold**, and **Font** itself.

• These features are used to change the appearance of text within the cells.

• However, the **Columns** option is not found on the Home ribbon; it is located on the **Page Layout** or **Insert** tab.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f13e2ad6582c16aa62a83672e2547ad20a01fddb61962a1acce42eb9a1a99caa.png] **Additional Information__**


• The Home ribbon also includes options for alignment, number formatting, cell styles, and editing tools.

• It is one of the most frequently used ribbons in Excel for day-to-day tasks.

• Understanding the different ribbons and their functions can greatly enhance productivity in Excel.

• Other ribbons in Excel include Insert, Page Layout, Formulas, Data, Review, and View, each containing specific tools and commands related to their respective purposes.

